Let \[ f(x) =
\begin{cases}
-x^2 & \text{if } x \geq 0,\\
x+10 & \text{if } x <0.
\end{cases}
\] Compute $f(f(f(f(f(2)))))$.

s:
Using polynomial long division:
\[
\begin{array}{c|cc cc}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{5x^2} & -5x & +3  \\
\cline{2-5}
2x+6 & 10x^3 & +20x^2&-9x&+6  \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{-10x^3} & -30x^2& \\ 
\cline{2-3}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{0} & -10x^2& -9x\\ 
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & +10x^2& +30x\\ 
\cline{3-4}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & 0& +21x & +6\\ 
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & -21x & -63\\ 
\cline{4-5}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & & -57\\ 
\end{array}
\]
The quotient from the division process is $\boxed{5x^2 - 5x + 3}$.

