s:
To simplify the expression $$(10^{0.4})(10^{0.6})(10^{0.3})(10^{0.2})(10^{0.5}),$$ we use the property of exponents where multiplying powers of the same base results in adding their exponents:
\begin{align*}
(10^{0.4})(10^{0.6})(10^{0.3})(10^{0.2})(10^{0.5}) &= 10^{0.4+0.6+0.3+0.2+0.5} \\
&= 10^{2.0} \\
&= \boxed{100}.
\end{align*}

